    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0438" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-02T10:00:00+08:00">March 2, 1947—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 2—2:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>416. Blake at Taipei reports March 2, 10 a.m. that Government removed refugees
                    from Consulate Saturday night just after 10 o’clock without incident and that
                    city appeared calm Sunday morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butterworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
